            <div xml:id="d877">

                <pb facs="0747" n="737" sameAs="frus:frus1949v08/pg737"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">123 Stuart, J. Leighton: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Stuart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-05-03T16:00:00+08:00">May 3, 1949—4 p.
                            m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received May 3—8:04 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>924. For first time today Ambassador permitted by guards at this compound to
                    visit Chancery. Embassy personnel also travelled about with little interference,
                    some in cars. A few were challenged on street but permitted proceed upon
                    identification.</p>
                <p>Repeated OffEmb Canton 344, Shanghai 419.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stuart</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
